<h1>time_seconds_to_bpm</h1>
<p>This function takes the length of a beat in seconds, and returns a beats-per-minute value.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">time_seconds_to_bpm(seconds);</p>
<table>
<colgroup>
<col/>
<col/>
<col/>
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>seconds</td>
<td><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></td>
<td>The seconds-per-beat value to convert into beats-per-minute</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">var _period = time_source_get_period(time_source);<br/>
var _bpm = time_seconds_to_bpm(_period);<br/>
<br/>
show_debug_message(_bpm);
</p>
<p>This function gets the period of a <span data-keyref="Type_Resource_TimeSource">Time Source</span>, converts it to BPM and prints that value to the output log.</p>
<p>This code follows the example for <a href="time_bpm_to_seconds.htm"><span class="inline">time_bpm_to_seconds()</span></a>.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
